This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-de1soc-music layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Purpose
=======

Installs the HPS side of the music player: the prebuilt hps_music_player
daemon, the bundled WAV library, and the systemd unit that starts the
daemon at every boot. Combined with meta-de1soc-fpga (which programs the
fabric first), the full HPS+FPGA stack is live from power-on with no
manual steps.

Contents
========

  conf/layer.conf
  recipes-music/hps-music-player/hps-music-player.bb
  recipes-music/hps-music-player/files/
      hps_music_player           Prebuilt ARM binary (cross-compiled with
                                 the Yocto SDK, see HPS_Workflow.md)
      hps_music_player.service   systemd unit
      music/                     WAV files installed to /mnt/music

How it works
============

hps_music_player.service starts the daemon after local-fs.target with
Restart=on-failure (2 s delay, max 5 restarts per 60 s). The restart
policy covers the early-boot window where the daemon may come up before
the FPGA is fully operating; ordering against fpga-load.service makes
this rare, the restart makes it harmless.

The daemon mmap()s the HPS-FPGA bridge shared memory, scans /mnt/music
for WAVs, and serves audio data to the Nios II following the protocol in
shared_protocol.h.

Verify on the board:

  systemctl status hps_music_player
  journalctl -u hps_music_player     # "shared mem mapped", "songs=N"
  ls -l /mnt/music

Updating the daemon or the music
================================

1. Cross-compile a new binary (HPS_Workflow.md) and replace
   recipes-music/hps-music-player/files/hps_music_player,
   and/or add/remove WAVs in files/music/
2. Rebuild:  bitbake hps-music-player -c cleansstate && bitbake hps-music-player
             bitbake core-image-minimal

The binary must stay in sync with the Nios II firmware whenever
shared_protocol.h changes — rebuild both sides from the same header.

Dependencies
============

  URI: https://github.com/altera-fpga/gsrd-socfpga.git
  branch: scarthgap

  Runtime: meta-de1soc-fpga (fpga-load.service must program the fabric
  before the daemon can map the bridge window)

Adding the meta-de1soc-music layer to your build
================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-de1soc-music'

Then install the recipe in conf/local.conf:

  IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " hps-music-player"

Patches
=======

This is a project-internal layer for the DE1-SoC FPGA Music Player
(TEC Computer Engineering). It is not submitted upstream.
